<title>USA: USDA boosts '97, '98 beef imports due to Argentina.</title>
<headline>USDA boosts '97, '98 beef imports due to Argentina.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department boosted Friday its forecast for 1997 and 1998 U.S. beef imports largely due to the recent go-ahead to Argentina to ship beef to the United States.</p>
<p>In its monthly world supply and demand report, USDA pegged 1997 U.S. beef imports at 2.376 billion lbs versus 2.341 billion lbs seen in June and forecast 1998 imports at 2.440 billion lbs, up from the prior estimate of 2.400 billion lbs.</p>
<p>Last month, USDA said it would allow fresh, chilled and frozen beef imports from Argentina as of August 25, ending a 67-year-old ban on beef shipments from that country.</p>
